.TH NSE 1 "April 2026" "ml.nse" "NSE Alpha Ranking System"
.SH NAME
nse-ingest, nse-features, nse-train, nse-backtest, nse-signal, nse-pipeline, nse-monitor \- NSE Daily Alpha Ranking System CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nse-ingest
[\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-features
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR [\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-train
[\fB\-\-n\-months\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-prod\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-recency\-half\-life\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-backtest
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR [\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-\-scenario\fR \fISCENARIO\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-signal
[\fB\-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-ingest\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-llm\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-pipeline
[\fB\-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-ingest\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-llm\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B nse-monitor
[\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-backfill\fR] [\fB\-\-drift\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The NSE Alpha Ranking System is a daily batch pipeline that ranks a small
universe of Nairobi Securities Exchange (NSE) equities by expected short-horizon
alpha after benchmark adjustment and trading costs.
.PP
MVP scope: long-only, top 5 names, human approval required, no autonomous
execution.
.PP
Current daily flow:
.IP 1. 4
\fBnse-ingest\fR \(em Aggregate OHLCV from the live \fInstocksdata\fR TimescaleDB
hypertable, fetch NSE market stats, company announcements, and macro data
(KES/USD, T-bills, CBK rate).
.IP 2.
\fBnse-features\fR \(em Compute \(ti50 features per ticker per day (returns,
volatility, liquidity, events, macro, LLM-extracted sentiment) and write to
\fIfeatures_daily\fR.
.IP 3.
\fBnse-train\fR \(em Walk-forward training of a LightGBM ranker on
\fIlabel_3d_net_alpha = future_3d_return \(mi benchmark_return \(mi round_trip_cost\fR.
.IP 4.
\fBnse-backtest\fR \(em Replay the saved model on historical data and print
Sharpe, drawdown, IC, hit-rate metrics.
.IP 5.
\fBnse-signal\fR \(em Run the current daily scoring pipeline and write the ranked signal report.
.IP 6.
\fBnse-pipeline\fR \(em Run the same daily pipeline entry point as \fBnse-signal\fR.
.IP 7.
\fBnse-monitor\fR \(em Track live IC, hit rate, and optional feature drift (PSI).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS nse-ingest
Download and store NSE prices, market stats, announcements, and macro data.
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR
Start date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Default: 60 days ago.
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR
End date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Re-download even if data is already cached.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging.
.SS nse-features
Build \fIfeatures_daily\fR table for a date range.
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR
Start date in YYYY-MM-DD format. \fBRequired.\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR
End date. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Force rebuild even if features already exist for the period.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging.
.SS nse-train
Walk-forward training; saves model artefact to \fImodels/saved/\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-n\-months\fR \fIN\fR
Number of walk-forward months to evaluate. Default: 12.
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\-only\fR
Skip walk-forward evaluation; train the production model only (faster).
.TP
\fB\-\-recency\-half\-life\fR \fIN\fR
Exponential sample-weight half-life in days (e.g.\& 90). Default: no weighting.
.TP
Behavior note
Production training includes a champion/challenger comparison against the
current saved \fBproduction\fR model on recent labelled data. The challenger
is deployed only if it outperforms the incumbent.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging.
.SS nse-backtest
Run backtest on historical data and print performance metrics.
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR
Backtest start date in YYYY-MM-DD format. \fBRequired.\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR
Backtest end date. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR
Model label to load from \fImodels/saved/\fR. Default: \fBproduction\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-scenario\fR \fISCENARIO\fR
Cost scenario: \fBoptimistic\fR (300 bps), \fBbase\fR (400 bps), or \fBstressed\fR (600 bps). Default: \fBbase\fR.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging.
.SS nse-signal
Score today\(aqs universe and write the ranked signal report.
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR
Signal date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR
Model label. Default: \fBproduction\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-ingest\fR
Skip data ingestion; use whatever is already in the database.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-llm\fR
Skip LLM extraction. Saves API cost.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging (default: on).
.TP
Behavior note
This command currently calls the same \fBrun_daily_pipeline()\fR implementation
as \fBnse-pipeline\fR.
.SS nse-pipeline
Full daily batch: ingest \(-> LLM \(-> features \(-> score \(-> risk \(-> report.
This is the single command to run each trading day.
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fIDATE\fR
Pipeline date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fILABEL\fR
Model label. Default: \fBproduction\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-ingest\fR
Skip data ingestion; use whatever is already in the database.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-llm\fR
Skip LLM extraction. Saves API cost.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging (default: on).
.SS nse-monitor
Live IC monitoring, hit rate, and optional feature drift check.
.TP
\fB\-\-start\fR \fIDATE\fR
Start date. Default: 1 year ago.
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fIDATE\fR
End date. Default: today.
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fIN\fR
Rolling IC window in trading days. Default: 20.
.TP
\fB\-\-backfill\fR
Run actuals backfill before reporting.
.TP
\fB\-\-drift\fR
Also run PSI (Population Stability Index) feature drift check.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable debug logging.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS One-time backfill and training
.nf
# Ingest 5 years of history
nse-ingest --start 2019-01-01 --end 2024-12-31

# Build features and labels
nse-features --start 2019-01-01 --end 2024-12-31

# Walk-forward evaluation + save production model
nse-train

# Quick validation
nse-backtest --start 2024-01-01 --scenario base
nse-backtest --start 2024-01-01 --scenario stressed
.fi
.SS Daily production run
.nf
# Full pipeline (run after NSE close or next morning)
nse-pipeline

# Skip LLM extraction to save API cost
nse-pipeline --skip-llm

# Replay a specific past date
nse-pipeline --date 2024-11-15

# Same daily pipeline, but skip ingestion
nse-signal --skip-ingest
.fi
.SS Monitoring
.nf
# Rolling 20-day IC and hit rate, last 90 days
nse-monitor --start 2025-01-01 --window 20

# Include PSI drift check
nse-monitor --drift

# Backfill outcome ledger then report
nse-monitor --backfill
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBANTHROPIC_API_KEY\fR
Required for LLM event extraction. Skip with \fB\-\-skip\-llm\fR.
.TP
\fBLLM_PROVIDER\fR, \fBANTHROPIC_MODEL\fR, \fBOLLAMA_MODEL\fR, \fBOLLAMA_BASE_URL\fR
Optional LLM provider configuration. Anthropic is the default provider.
.TP
\fBDB_HOST\fR, \fBDB_PORT\fR, \fBDB_NAME\fR, \fBDB_USER\fR, \fBDB_PASS\fR, \fBDB_SSLMODE\fR
Connection settings for the \fIml_nse\fR ML pipeline database.
.TP
\fBDB_NAME2\fR
Name of the live scraper database (default: \fBnse\fR) containing the
\fIstocksdata\fR TimescaleDB hypertable.
.TP
Runtime note
If \fBDB_HOST\fR is not set, the application falls back to a local SQLite
database at \fIdata/nse.db\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI.env\fR
Environment variables file, loaded automatically at startup.
.TP
\fImodels/saved/ranker_production.pkl\fR
Serialised production model artefact written by \fBnse-train\fR and read
by \fBnse-signal\fR, \fBnse-pipeline\fR, and \fBnse-backtest\fR.
.TP
\fIreports/output/signal_YYYY-MM-DD.csv\fR
Daily ranked signal report (CSV).
.TP
\fIreports/output/signal_YYYY-MM-DD.json\fR
Daily ranked signal report (JSON).
.TP
\fIlogs/\fR
Log files written during pipeline runs.
.TP
\fIscripts/diagnose_signals.py\fR
Diagnostic utility for checking signal coverage, backfill status, data-quality
flags, and label distribution.
.TP
\fIscripts/completions/nse_completions.bash\fR
Bash tab-completion. Source in \fI~/.bashrc\fR.
.TP
\fIscripts/completions/_nse\fR
Zsh tab-completion. Add parent directory to \fIfpath\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python (1),
.BR pip (1)
.PP
Project repository: \fIml.nse\fR
.br
Technical report: \fIresearch/RESULTS_SUMMARY.md\fR
.SH NOTES
This system is an advisory tool only. All signals require human review
before execution. No trade is placed autonomously.
.PP
Universe: SCOM, EQTY, KCB, COOP, BAT, ABSA, SCBK, JUB, EABL, BAMB, NMG, BRIT
(configurable in \fInse/config.py\fR).
.PP
Risk limits: max 5 positions, 20% single-name weight, 40% daily turnover,
15% drawdown kill-switch, minimum model score 0.55.
.PP
Implementation note: the primary training label still uses the base 500 bps
round-trip cost assumption on a 3-trading-day horizon. See
\fIdocs/operations.md\fR for the current discussion of that limitation.
